+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm start` to serve the application. Run `pnpm test` for automated DOM and WebMCP integration tests; no browser is required.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The homepage registers these tools using the native `document.modelContext.registerTool()` API:
+
+| Tool | Input | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `list_seasonal_favorites` | `{ "query": "oat" }` (query is optional) | Reads and optionally filters the visible drink names and descriptions, returning details links. |
+| `list_site_pages` | `{}` | Returns destination identifiers, titles, and URLs from the page. |
+| `navigate_to_page` | `{ "page": "menu" }` | Opens an advertised destination in the current tab. |
+
+Tools read the existing HTML so their results reflect the visible content. Inputs are validated at execution time, and invalid requests return structured errors. Navigation uses the same destinations as the ordinary links; it does not implement the linked pages or submit purchases. Logout remains a manual link and is excluded from agent navigation.
+
+Use a WebMCP-capable browser in a secure context (HTTPS, or a trustworthy localhost development origin). Agents provided by the browser or extensions can discover registered tools. Browsers without `document.modelContext` retain the normal page and links; no polyfill or external service is installed.
+
+Registration uses an AbortController for cleanup, including rollback on partial registration failure. `registerDailyGrindTools(document)` returns a `dispose()` function after successful registration. Tools live for the lifetime of the homepage document, with no cross-origin exposure requested.
+
+The implementation follows the current [Chrome WebMCP imperative API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api), using `document.modelContext` and registration signals rather than deprecated navigator APIs.
